## What this command does

It brings this platform's existing mhk files up to the format of the installed mhk, {{version}}, by applying the migration notes released since they were last migrated. Then it records {{version}} in `.mhk/version.json`. It is the fast path after updating mhk:

- It never scans the code, never invokes a discovery subagent, and never runs builds, tests, installs or generators. A note that needs new evidence names the command to rerun instead.
- It changes only mhk-owned text: the mhk blocks in `{{root_file}}` and the owned topics in `{{rules_dir}}/`. Unlike the other workflows, it may edit every mhk block of this platform, but only as a note directs. Text outside mhk-owned files is reported, never edited.
- It never sets up a layer that isn't there: {{rules_command}} and {{memory_command}} do that, and the doctor lists layers that are not set up. Converting an older form of a layer that is there is a migration, not a setup.
- It changes only this platform's files and this platform's entry in `.mhk/version.json`.

